    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "title": "Unmasking Data: Revealing the Hidden Bias Within",
      "description": "",
      "date": "Jul 28, 2023",
      "read_time": "3 min read",
      "author": "Farhana Alarakhiya",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "43-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In today's world, digital technology plays a crucial role in improving our lives. As automation continues to grow, we are faced with a significant challenge. For 49.75% of the world's population and 50.2% of Africa's population, this challenge is particularly pronounced due to the existing patriarchal societal structures. Let's explore the impact of data bias in technology and its implications for women in Africa, while shedding light on potential solutions for a more equitable future."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Land Inheritance for Women in Africa "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "One striking example of gender inequality in Africa lies in the realm of land inheritance. Meet Rachel Korir, who fought a forty-year battle to gain access to just one acre of her parents' 42-acre land. Despite being dominant in agriculture, women in Africa face numerous obstacles in obtaining land ownership. Shockingly, only 10.3% of all title deeds in Kenya, are issued to women, with less than 2% of that land belonging to them. This gender bias grows exponentially when codefied in technology."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Gender Gap in Healthcare Research "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Healthcare studies predominantly focus on men, neglecting the specific health needs of women leading to insufficient research on women's issues. In low- and middle-income countries (LMICs), the gender gap becomes even more pronounced. Within my department at AKU, we've built a large health repository of anonymous data. The data reveals that women are more likely to report adverse reactions to medication and be hospitalized due to them."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Data Bias in Technology "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "It is essential to recognize that the issue does not lie within technology itself but rather in the data bias that exists within it. Algorithms operate based on the data they are fed. Let me paint a picture, an algorithm is written to make a decision based on our world population. The code for this algorithm says to look at all data, but the access to 'all data' is made up of 90% men and only 10% women. The algorithm considers this to be the world population and would essentially amplify male data and basically make women invisible."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Translated into practice, when used to hire a new employee, males will be favoured. In selection for credit, males would be the lower risk option; public services, male-focused services would dominate. "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "As technology's influence on our daily lives grows, so does the amplification of such biases. Addressing data bias and fostering an inclusive tech landscape is critical."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Steps Towards an Equitable Future "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "To dismantle the barriers perpetuated by data bias, several crucial steps must be taken. First, we need to acknowledge and address the bias in data collection. Second, we need AI to be explainable. Understanding how algorithms work, and are built by diverse teams that ensure representative data is vital to combating bias. Lastly, lobbying governments and policymakers to implement programmes and policies that address data bias is essential for scalable widespread change."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "An Equitable World: Rachel's Story Reimagined "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In an equitable future, Rachel and her sisters not only secure rights to land and title deeds but witness a cultural shift where such ownership becomes the norm. Financial literacy programmes empower women, while subsidized smartphone initiatives not only grant them access to the internet but ensure female data is represented. Rachel and her sisters now have access to credit, thanks to changes in lending algorithms that recognize women entrepreneurs' higher revenue generation. Moreover, technology caters to the unique needs of women, ensuring their meaningful inclusion in the digital world."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 3
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A Call for Change "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "As we envision an equitable future, we must acknowledge the pivotal role data bias plays in perpetuating gender inequality. By addressing bias in data collection, embracing explainable AI, and advocating for comprehensive policies, we can pave the way for a future where technology becomes a catalyst for gender equality rather than an enabler of discrimination."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
